# What the standby discard model stands for. .agents/skills/standby-discard says how to keep it true:
# its Coverage record maps each model action to the code below.
#
# sync: the commit whose code the model was last confirmed to describe. Move it only as the
# skill's step 1 and full run say. 38bd550c95 is main when SLNT-1053 moved it: mend#1727's squash,
# whose covered changes (SLNT-1044) the line before already accounted for, and nothing else in the
# covered files. SLNT-1053 changed the model with the code: the launch's re-plan is asked again
# and, when no ask answered, the standby's own status decides adoption (AReplanOk, AReplanFail,
# AIdentify); a session's drain discards a claimed standby whose re-plan never took and in which no
# process ever ran (discardStandbyNeverClaimed: GLook, GIdentify,
# GDiscard, KeptRetry), with joins modelled (JEnter, JLook). SessionProcessesRepo joins the
# covered files for existsForWorkspace. Its second round (the box check of mend#1741) added the
# owner's Stop during the asks (Stop, AgentStarts) and bound the session's channel again before
# the cold launch, which no action models (the channel is not in the model).
# c34dea602e is main when SLNT-1063 moved it: SLNT-1053's squash (d1039eaf1d), which changed the
# model with the code, and nothing else in the covered files. SLNT-1063 (mend#1756) then changed
# engine.ts only outside the covered functions: every workspace create's env and each person's
# process env carry MEND_ORIGIN, and the workspace note names it; no action models either. The
# full TLC run on its head, dde8b8acd6, had every row as expected.
# 591a9e6e3b is the SLNT-895 feature branch on main after SLNT-1063, when it moved the line. Its
# covered changes deliver an imported conversation at a session's first protocol launch:
# conversationOf's home, launchProtocol's resume id and prepareImportedConversation. They make no
# hot-pool, claim, retire, drain or session-process call, so no action models them. Full TLC run at
# 591a9e6e3b: every row as expected.
# 7a2f304a37 is the SLNT-1113 branch on main after SLNT-895's squash, whose covered changes the
# line before accounted for. SLNT-1113 changed engine.ts only outside the covered functions: after
# each head refresh (refreshChangeHead) the engine counts the change's files through WorktreeReads
# in a forked fiber and keeps the count on the change row. It makes no hot-pool, claim, retire,
# drain or session-process call, so no action models it. Full TLC run at 225d463a4c, the same
# engine.ts before a rebase: every row as expected.
# 646dea54b8 is the SLNT-1130 branch on main at 494c29441c. SLNT-1130 changed engine.ts only
# outside the covered functions: a person's Stop session (`stopSession`) runs `stop` unchanged,
# then, when no other session in the workspace is running (`stopSessionReachOf`, a read), stops the
# workspace's Services and shells and asks `stopWorkspaceIfUnleased` again. Each of those is a path
# Stop followed by Stop services already took; it makes no hot-pool, claim, retire or discard call,
# so no action models it. Full tlx run at 646dea54b8: every row as expected (`code` 129,386,795
# states, 351 s on four workers).
# 68e02def24 is the SLNT-1149 branch on main at 06b0294959. SLNT-1149 changed engine.ts only
# outside the covered functions: shared control can go to one person (sharedControlUserIds), so
# neverShared, conversationOf, the shared steering decide (sharedControlFor, protocolHooksFor's fork
# path), the person a protocol start runs as, and the steerer's login refusal (steeringRefusalOf,
# submitTurnChecked, sendMessage, steerTurn) read who may steer through canSteerSession and
# sharesControl. None makes a hot-pool, claim, retire, drain, stop or session-process call, so no
# action models them. Full tlx run at 68e02def24: every row as expected (`code` 129,386,795
# states, 250 s on four workers).
# b2165b19d0 is the SLNT-1155 branch (a project's workspace image is its own copy) on main at
# a8ea15ce85; its covered files are byte-for-byte those of c25699aa2f, the same branch on 5a2a9426d. Its covered changes are in engine.ts only: every read of a project's image
# (`hotInputsFor`, the launch's create, the person-layout image reads, the person dotfiles' image)
# reads `project.workspaceImage` itself instead of falling back to the organization's settings, and
# the engine no longer needs `SettingsRepo`. Which image a standby is built from feeds its
# fingerprint, as before; no claim, retire, drain, discard or session-process call changed, so no
# action models it. Full tlx run at c25699aa2f: every row as expected (`code` 129,386,795 states,
# 423 s on four workers).
# 6f91cc5491 is the SLNT-1196 branch on main at f019cbb214. Its covered change is one line in
# engine.ts, outside every covered function's modelled steps: after a launch, the session line no
# longer says that an image's per-person users are still being checked (UNKNOWN_IMAGE_REASON). It
# writes the session's summary only; no claim, retire, drain, discard, stop or session-process call
# changed, so no action models it. Full tlx run at 6f91cc5491: every row as expected (`code`
# 129,386,795 states, 332 s on four workers).
# 1e50a49f7d is the SLNT-1205 branch on main at b165a2b0ed, whose covered files carry nothing since
# 6f91cc5491 but SLNT-1196's squash, which the line before accounted for. SLNT-1205 changed engine.ts
# only inside `stop`'s choice of the shells it closes: an agent whose terminal the stop closed, and
# whose end the PTY watcher recorded first, counts as one the stop ended, so the session's shells
# stay. It makes no hot-pool, claim, retire, discard or drain call, and no action models a shell, so
# no action models it. Full tlx run at 1e50a49f7d: every row as expected (`code` 129,386,795 states,
# 218 s on four workers).
sync 1e50a49f7dc337b2a1d3a91c314e88924aee6361

model StandbyDiscard.tla
model MCStandbyDiscard.tla
model check.sh

path packages/db/src/repos/hot-workspaces.ts
path packages/db/src/repos/session-processes.ts
path packages/sessions/src/engine.ts
path packages/sessions/src/capture-channel.ts

# How long check.sh may run on CI's four-core runner before formal.mjs stops it and fails
# naming this model (SLNT-1065, SLNT-1081). With tlx the full bounds took 8.4 minutes on CI
# (run 44103197639, `code` 486 s) and --quick 13 seconds. GitHub's four-core runner is not one
# speed: TLC ran 1.5 times slower on a slow host (SLNT-1065), so a slow host needs about 12.5
# minutes. budget-full is twice that; CI's formal job allows 10 minutes more for setup and a tlx
# build when its cache has none.
budget-quick 5
budget-full 25
